// Differential 78 — Level-B `audio_score` (M0.8 E6 audio / adaptive music).
// Serialized-IR parity: the interpreter BUILDS the audio_score descriptor, the
// cooked Zig EMITS it; both serialize through the shared canonical serializer
// (`descriptor_types.zig`) and must produce byte-identical dumps (LEVEL-B PROOF
// CONTRACT). The grammar §12.1 shape WINS over validation-ecs §20: STRING-named,
// `score_property`s (bare `tempo: 90` — STRICT, the ability ruling-15 precedent,
// the example's `@unit(.bpm)` omitted, KB-patch part2 §25 at close), `section`s
// (plain `key: value` props + the `can_transition_to` section list + the
// `on_finish "->" IDENT` target), and a `stems` block. DELIVER: E1720 (reshaped
// "no section AND no stems"), E1721 DuplicateSectionName, E1722 DuplicateStemName,
// E1726 (rekeyed onto can_transition_to / on_finish targets — every target is a
// declared section here), E1728 TempoInvalid. RESERVED: E1724 StemActiveUnknown /
// E1725 SectionDurationInvalid (no stems_active / duration in this shape).
// DEFERRED: E1723 / E1727 / W1720 / W1721 (asset + transition-point catalogues,
// heuristics — `transition_points` omitted). Section names + targets are
// TYPE_IDENT-shaped (the ratified name-position deviation). No music plays.
audio_score "exploration" {
  tempo: 90

  section Calm {
    clips: ["music/explore_calm_a.ogg", "music/explore_calm_b.ogg"]
    loop: true
    can_transition_to: [Tension, Combat]
  }

  section Tension {
    intro: "music/tension_intro.ogg"
    loop: "music/tension_loop.ogg"
    on_finish: -> Combat
  }

  section Combat {
    loop: "music/combat_loop.ogg"
  }

  stems {
    bass: { clip: "music/combat_bass.ogg", always_active: true }
    drums: { clip: "music/combat_drums.ogg" }
  }
}
